IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `eia-core`
IMPORT `ei2-nouns`

-- Employment Insurance Act (S.C. 1996, c. 23), ss 38 to 41.1: penalties for claimants and others acting for them,
-- penalties for employers, directors and agents, the limits on imposing a penalty, rescission or reduction, and
-- warnings. Piece ei2. Text: the unofficial plain-text rendering of the Justice Laws consolidation current to
-- 2026-09-30. Seat: the claimant (ss 38, 40, 41, 41.1). The employer's provisions (s 39) are encoded here for what they
-- decide and are not asked in the claimant's seat layer; an employer seat would ask them.
--
-- Relations (Hohfeld). A penalty provision gives the Commission a power to impose a penalty; the person it may be imposed
-- on (the claimant, a person acting for them, the employer, a director or agent) is under the correlative liability.
-- Section 40 is the person's immunity from a penalty after a prosecution has begun or time has run (the Commission's
-- disability); s 41 and s 41.1 are further powers of the Commission over the same person.
--
-- The Commission "becomes aware of facts that in its opinion establish" the act: its opinion is a BOOLEAN input, and each
-- act is a BOOLEAN fact about what the person did. The Commission's rate of weekly benefits, the s 19(3) deduction and the
-- maximum rate of weekly benefits are out of range (sections 14 and 19, piece ei1; the maximum rate is s 14 and the
-- Regulations): plain NUMBER inputs.

§ `Section 38 - penalties for claimants and persons acting for them`

-- (1): "The Commission may impose on a claimant, or any other person acting for a claimant, a penalty for each of the
-- following acts or omissions if the Commission becomes aware of facts that in its opinion establish that the claimant
-- or other person has (a) ... (h) ...". The eight acts are alternatives (paragraph (g) ends "; or").
-- src:829 | Penalty for claimants, etc.
-- src:830 | 38 (1) The Commission may impose on a claimant, or any other person acting for a claimant, a penalty for each of the following acts or omissions if the Commission becomes aware of facts that in its opinion establish that the claimant or other person has
-- src:831 | (a) in relation to a claim for benefits, made a representation that the claimant or other person knew was false or misleading;
-- src:832 | (b) being required under this Act or the regulations to provide information, provided information or made a representation that the claimant or other person knew was false or misleading;
-- src:833 | (c) knowingly failed to declare to the Commission all or some of the claimant’s earnings for a period determined under the regulations for which the claimant claimed benefits;
-- src:834 | (d) made a claim or declaration that the claimant or other person knew was false or misleading because of the non-disclosure of facts;
-- src:835 | (e) being the payee of a special warrant, knowingly negotiated or attempted to negotiate it for benefits to which the claimant was not entitled;
-- src:836 | (f) knowingly failed to return a special warrant or the amount of the warrant or any excess amount, as required by section 44;
-- src:837 | (g) imported or exported a document issued by the Commission, or had it imported or exported, for the purpose of defrauding or deceiving the Commission; or
-- src:838 | (h) participated in, assented to or acquiesced in an act or omission mentioned in paragraphs (a) to (g).
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 38(1) (src:829-838)
GIVEN `the Commission becomes aware of facts that in its opinion establish an act or omission mentioned in subsection 38(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `in relation to a claim for benefits, made a representation that the claimant or other person knew was false or misleading` IS A BOOLEAN
      `being required under the Act or the regulations to provide information, provided information or made a representation that the claimant or other person knew was false or misleading` IS A BOOLEAN
      `knowingly failed to declare to the Commission all or some of the claimant's earnings for a period determined under the regulations for which the claimant claimed benefits` IS A BOOLEAN
      `made a claim or declaration that the claimant or other person knew was false or misleading because of the non-disclosure of facts` IS A BOOLEAN
      `being the payee of a special warrant, knowingly negotiated or attempted to negotiate it for benefits to which the claimant was not entitled` IS A BOOLEAN
      `knowingly failed to return a special warrant or the amount of the warrant or any excess amount, as required by section 44` IS A BOOLEAN
      `imported or exported a document issued by the Commission, or had it imported or exported, for the purpose of defrauding or deceiving the Commission` IS A BOOLEAN
      `participated in, assented to or acquiesced in an act or omission mentioned in paragraphs 38(1)(a) to (g)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 38(1) the Commission may impose a penalty on the claimant or a person acting for the claimant` IF
        `the Commission becomes aware of facts that in its opinion establish an act or omission mentioned in subsection 38(1)`
    AND (   `in relation to a claim for benefits, made a representation that the claimant or other person knew was false or misleading`
         OR `being required under the Act or the regulations to provide information, provided information or made a representation that the claimant or other person knew was false or misleading`
         OR `knowingly failed to declare to the Commission all or some of the claimant's earnings for a period determined under the regulations for which the claimant claimed benefits`
         OR `made a claim or declaration that the claimant or other person knew was false or misleading because of the non-disclosure of facts`
         OR `being the payee of a special warrant, knowingly negotiated or attempted to negotiate it for benefits to which the claimant was not entitled`
         OR `knowingly failed to return a special warrant or the amount of the warrant or any excess amount, as required by section 44`
         OR `imported or exported a document issued by the Commission, or had it imported or exported, for the purpose of defrauding or deceiving the Commission`
         OR `participated in, assented to or acquiesced in an act or omission mentioned in paragraphs 38(1)(a) to (g)`)

-- (2): "The Commission may set the amount of the penalty for each act or omission at not more than (a) three times the
-- claimant's rate of weekly benefits; (b) if the penalty is imposed under paragraph (1)(c), (i) three times the amount of
-- the deduction from the claimant's benefits under subsection 19(3), and (ii) three times the benefits that would have been
-- paid to the claimant for the period mentioned in that paragraph if the deduction had not been made under subsection 19(3)
-- or the claimant had not been disentitled or disqualified from receiving benefits; or (c) three times the maximum rate of
-- weekly benefits in effect when the act or omission occurred, if no benefit period was established."
-- The four ceilings, one rule each; how they combine is fork ei2-F8 in NOTES.md.
-- src:839 | Maximum penalty
-- src:840 | (2) The Commission may set the amount of the penalty for each act or omission at not more than
-- src:841 | (a) three times the claimant’s rate of weekly benefits;
-- src:842 | (b) if the penalty is imposed under paragraph (1)(c),
-- src:843 | (i) three times the amount of the deduction from the claimant’s benefits under subsection 19(3), and
-- src:844 | (ii) three times the benefits that would have been paid to the claimant for the period mentioned in that paragraph if the deduction had not been made under subsection 19(3) or the claimant had not been disentitled or disqualified from receiving benefits; or
-- src:845 | (c) three times the maximum rate of weekly benefits in effect when the act or omission occurred, if no benefit period was established.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 38(2)(a) (src:839-841)
GIVEN `the claimant's rate of weekly benefits` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `s 38(2)(a) three times the claimant's rate of weekly benefits` IS 3 TIMES `the claimant's rate of weekly benefits`

@ref Employment Insurance Act s 38(2)(b)(i) (src:842-843)
GIVEN `the amount of the deduction from the claimant's benefits under subsection 19(3)` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `s 38(2)(b)(i) three times the amount of the deduction under subsection 19(3)` IS 3 TIMES `the amount of the deduction from the claimant's benefits under subsection 19(3)`

@ref Employment Insurance Act s 38(2)(b)(ii) (src:844)
GIVEN `the benefits that would have been paid for the period if the deduction had not been made or the claimant had not been disentitled or disqualified` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `s 38(2)(b)(ii) three times the benefits that would have been paid` IS 3 TIMES `the benefits that would have been paid for the period if the deduction had not been made or the claimant had not been disentitled or disqualified`

@ref Employment Insurance Act s 38(2)(c) (src:845)
GIVEN `the maximum rate of weekly benefits in effect when the act or omission occurred` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `s 38(2)(c) three times the maximum rate of weekly benefits in effect when the act or omission occurred` IS 3 TIMES `the maximum rate of weekly benefits in effect when the act or omission occurred`

-- The most the Commission may set for one act or omission: with no benefit period, limb (c); with one, limb (a) and,
-- for a penalty under paragraph (1)(c), limb (b), whose two parts joined by "and" both bind (the lesser of the two); the
-- limbs are alternatives ("; or (c)"), so the largest limb that applies is the most (fork ei2-F8).
-- src:839 | Maximum penalty
-- src:840 | (2) The Commission may set the amount of the penalty for each act or omission at not more than
-- src:841 | (a) three times the claimant’s rate of weekly benefits;
-- src:842 | (b) if the penalty is imposed under paragraph (1)(c),
-- src:843 | (i) three times the amount of the deduction from the claimant’s benefits under subsection 19(3), and
-- src:844 | (ii) three times the benefits that would have been paid to the claimant for the period mentioned in that paragraph if the deduction had not been made under subsection 19(3) or the claimant had not been disentitled or disqualified from receiving benefits; or
-- src:845 | (c) three times the maximum rate of weekly benefits in effect when the act or omission occurred, if no benefit period was established.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 38(2) (src:839-845)
GIVEN `a benefit period was established for the claimant` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the penalty is imposed under paragraph 38(1)(c)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claimant's rate of weekly benefits` IS A NUMBER
      `the amount of the deduction from the claimant's benefits under subsection 19(3)` IS A NUMBER
      `the benefits that would have been paid for the period if the deduction had not been made or the claimant had not been disentitled or disqualified` IS A NUMBER
      `the maximum rate of weekly benefits in effect when the act or omission occurred` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `s 38(2) the most the Commission may set as the amount of the penalty` IS
    IF (NOT `a benefit period was established for the claimant`)
    THEN `s 38(2)(c) three times the maximum rate of weekly benefits in effect when the act or omission occurred` `the maximum rate of weekly benefits in effect when the act or omission occurred`
    ELSE IF `the penalty is imposed under paragraph 38(1)(c)`
         THEN IF `limb b` AT LEAST `limb a` THEN `limb b` ELSE `limb a`
         ELSE `limb a`
    WHERE
        `limb a` MEANS `s 38(2)(a) three times the claimant's rate of weekly benefits` `the claimant's rate of weekly benefits`
        `limb b` MEANS
            IF `s 38(2)(b)(i) three times the amount of the deduction under subsection 19(3)` `the amount of the deduction from the claimant's benefits under subsection 19(3)` AT MOST `s 38(2)(b)(ii) three times the benefits that would have been paid` `the benefits that would have been paid for the period if the deduction had not been made or the claimant had not been disentitled or disqualified`
            THEN `s 38(2)(b)(i) three times the amount of the deduction under subsection 19(3)` `the amount of the deduction from the claimant's benefits under subsection 19(3)`
            ELSE `s 38(2)(b)(ii) three times the benefits that would have been paid` `the benefits that would have been paid for the period if the deduction had not been made or the claimant had not been disentitled or disqualified`

-- (3): "For greater certainty, weeks of regular benefits that are repaid as a result of an act or omission mentioned in
-- subsection (1) are deemed to be weeks of regular benefits paid for the purposes of the application of subsection
-- 145(2)." Section 145(2) is piece ei4's.
-- src:846 | Determination under subsection 145(2)
-- src:847 | (3) For greater certainty, weeks of regular benefits that are repaid as a result of an act or omission mentioned in subsection (1) are deemed to be weeks of regular benefits paid for the purposes of the application of subsection 145(2).
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 38(3) (src:846-847)
GIVEN `weeks of regular benefits are repaid as a result of an act or omission mentioned in subsection 38(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 38(3) the repaid weeks are deemed to be weeks of regular benefits paid for the purposes of subsection 145(2)` IS
    IF `weeks of regular benefits are repaid as a result of an act or omission mentioned in subsection 38(1)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

§ `Section 39 - penalties for employers and others`

-- (1): "The Commission may impose on an employer, or any other person acting for an employer or pretending to be or act
-- for an employer, a penalty for each of the following acts if the Commission becomes aware of facts that in its opinion
-- establish that the employer or other person has (a) ... (e) ...".
-- src:848 | Penalty for employers, etc.
-- src:849 | 39 (1) The Commission may impose on an employer, or any other person acting for an employer or pretending to be or act for an employer, a penalty for each of the following acts if the Commission becomes aware of facts that in its opinion establish that the employer or other person has
-- src:850 | (a) made, in relation to any matter arising under this Act, a representation that the employer or other person knew was false or misleading;
-- src:851 | (b) being required under this Act or the regulations to provide information, provided information or made a representation that the employer or other person knew was false or misleading;
-- src:852 | (c) in relation to any matter arising under this Act, made a declaration that the employer or other person knew was false or misleading because of the non-disclosure of facts;
-- src:853 | (d) imported or exported a document issued by the Commission, or had it imported or exported, for the purpose of defrauding or deceiving the Commission; or
-- src:854 | (e) participated in, assented to or acquiesced in an act mentioned in paragraphs (a) to (d).
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 39(1) (src:848-854)
GIVEN `the Commission becomes aware of facts that in its opinion establish an act mentioned in subsection 39(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `made, in relation to any matter arising under the Act, a representation that the employer or other person knew was false or misleading` IS A BOOLEAN
      `being required under the Act or the regulations to provide information, provided information or made a representation that the employer or other person knew was false or misleading` IS A BOOLEAN
      `in relation to any matter arising under the Act, made a declaration that the employer or other person knew was false or misleading because of the non-disclosure of facts` IS A BOOLEAN
      `imported or exported a document issued by the Commission, or had it imported or exported, for the purpose of defrauding or deceiving the Commission` IS A BOOLEAN
      `participated in, assented to or acquiesced in an act mentioned in paragraphs 39(1)(a) to (d)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 39(1) the Commission may impose a penalty on the employer or a person acting for the employer` IF
        `the Commission becomes aware of facts that in its opinion establish an act mentioned in subsection 39(1)`
    AND (   `made, in relation to any matter arising under the Act, a representation that the employer or other person knew was false or misleading`
         OR `being required under the Act or the regulations to provide information, provided information or made a representation that the employer or other person knew was false or misleading`
         OR `in relation to any matter arising under the Act, made a declaration that the employer or other person knew was false or misleading because of the non-disclosure of facts`
         OR `imported or exported a document issued by the Commission, or had it imported or exported, for the purpose of defrauding or deceiving the Commission`
         OR `participated in, assented to or acquiesced in an act mentioned in paragraphs 39(1)(a) to (d)`)

-- (3): "If the Commission becomes aware of facts that in its opinion establish that a corporation has committed an act
-- described in subsection (1) and that any officer, director or agent of the corporation has directed, authorized,
-- assented to, acquiesced in or participated in the act, the Commission may impose a penalty on the officer, director or
-- agent, whether or not a penalty has been imposed on the corporation."
-- src:857 | Officers, etc., of corporations
-- src:858 | (3) If the Commission becomes aware of facts that in its opinion establish that a corporation has committed an act described in subsection (1) and that any officer, director or agent of the corporation has directed, authorized, assented to, acquiesced in or participated in the act, the Commission may impose a penalty on the officer, director or agent, whether or not a penalty has been imposed on the corporation.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 39(3) (src:857-858)
GIVEN `the Commission becomes aware of facts that in its opinion establish that a corporation has committed an act described in subsection 39(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Commission becomes aware of facts that in its opinion establish that an officer, director or agent of the corporation has directed, authorized, assented to, acquiesced in or participated in the act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 39(3) the Commission may impose a penalty on an officer, director or agent of the corporation` IF
        `the Commission becomes aware of facts that in its opinion establish that a corporation has committed an act described in subsection 39(1)`
    AND `the Commission becomes aware of facts that in its opinion establish that an officer, director or agent of the corporation has directed, authorized, assented to, acquiesced in or participated in the act`

-- (2), (4), (5): the amount. (2) "not more than nine times the maximum rate of weekly benefits in effect when the penalty is
-- imposed". (4) "Notwithstanding subsection (2), if the act involves the provision of information about any matter on which
-- the fulfilment of conditions for the qualification and entitlement for receiving or continuing to receive benefits
-- depends, the Commission may set the amount of the penalty at not more than the greater of (a) $12,000, and (b) the amount
-- of the penalty imposed under section 38 on any person who made a claim for benefits based on the information provided."
-- (5) "Notwithstanding subsection (2), the Commission may set the amount of the penalty at an amount required or authorized
-- by the regulations if the act is a major contravention, as defined under the regulations." The regulations are made
-- under s 54(g.1) (a maximum of $25,000) and are not among the inputs: an input amount.
-- src:855 | Maximum penalty
-- src:856 | (2) The Commission may set the amount of the penalty for each act at not more than nine times the maximum rate of weekly benefits in effect when the penalty is imposed.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 39(2) (src:855-856)
GIVEN `the maximum rate of weekly benefits in effect when the penalty is imposed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `s 39(2) nine times the maximum rate of weekly benefits in effect when the penalty is imposed` IS 9 TIMES `the maximum rate of weekly benefits in effect when the penalty is imposed`

-- src:859 | Contravention of information requirements
-- src:860 | (4) Notwithstanding subsection (2), if the act involves the provision of information about any matter on which the fulfilment of conditions for the qualification and entitlement for receiving or continuing to receive benefits depends, the Commission may set the amount of the penalty at not more than the greater of
-- src:861 | (a) $12,000, and
-- src:862 | (b) the amount of the penalty imposed under section 38 on any person who made a claim for benefits based on the information provided.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 39(4) (src:859-862)
GIVEN `the amount of the penalty imposed under section 38 on any person who made a claim for benefits based on the information provided` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `s 39(4) the greater of $12,000 and the penalty imposed under section 38` IS
    IF `the amount of the penalty imposed under section 38 on any person who made a claim for benefits based on the information provided` AT LEAST 12000
    THEN `the amount of the penalty imposed under section 38 on any person who made a claim for benefits based on the information provided`
    ELSE 12000

-- The most the Commission may set for one act: (2), unless (4) or (5) applies, in which case "notwithstanding subsection (2)"
-- the greater of the amounts that do apply (fork ei2-F9). The amount for a major contravention is the regulations' own.
-- src:855 | Maximum penalty
-- src:856 | (2) The Commission may set the amount of the penalty for each act at not more than nine times the maximum rate of weekly benefits in effect when the penalty is imposed.
-- src:857 | Officers, etc., of corporations
-- src:858 | (3) If the Commission becomes aware of facts that in its opinion establish that a corporation has committed an act described in subsection (1) and that any officer, director or agent of the corporation has directed, authorized, assented to, acquiesced in or participated in the act, the Commission may impose a penalty on the officer, director or agent, whether or not a penalty has been imposed on the corporation.
-- src:859 | Contravention of information requirements
-- src:860 | (4) Notwithstanding subsection (2), if the act involves the provision of information about any matter on which the fulfilment of conditions for the qualification and entitlement for receiving or continuing to receive benefits depends, the Commission may set the amount of the penalty at not more than the greater of
-- src:861 | (a) $12,000, and
-- src:862 | (b) the amount of the penalty imposed under section 38 on any person who made a claim for benefits based on the information provided.
-- src:863 | Major contraventions
-- src:864 | (5) Notwithstanding subsection (2), the Commission may set the amount of the penalty at an amount required or authorized by the regulations if the act is a major contravention, as defined under the regulations.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 39(2), s 39(4), s 39(5) (src:855-864)
GIVEN `the maximum rate of weekly benefits in effect when the penalty is imposed` IS A NUMBER
      `the act involves the provision of information about a matter on which the fulfilment of conditions for qualification and entitlement depends` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the amount of the penalty imposed under section 38 on any person who made a claim for benefits based on the information provided` IS A NUMBER
      `the act is a major contravention as defined under the regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the amount required or authorized by the regulations for the major contravention` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `s 39 the most the Commission may set as the amount of the penalty` IS
    BRANCH IF     `the act involves the provision of information about a matter on which the fulfilment of conditions for qualification and entitlement depends`
              AND `the act is a major contravention as defined under the regulations`
              THEN IF `limb 4` AT LEAST `limb 5` THEN `limb 4` ELSE `limb 5`
           IF `the act involves the provision of information about a matter on which the fulfilment of conditions for qualification and entitlement depends`
              THEN `limb 4`
           IF `the act is a major contravention as defined under the regulations`
              THEN `limb 5`
           OTHERWISE `s 39(2) nine times the maximum rate of weekly benefits in effect when the penalty is imposed` `the maximum rate of weekly benefits in effect when the penalty is imposed`
    WHERE
        `limb 4` MEANS `s 39(4) the greater of $12,000 and the penalty imposed under section 38` `the amount of the penalty imposed under section 38 on any person who made a claim for benefits based on the information provided`
        `limb 5` MEANS `the amount required or authorized by the regulations for the major contravention`

§ `Sections 40, 41 and 41.1 - limits, rescission and warnings`

-- 40: "A penalty shall not be imposed under section 38 or 39 if (a) a prosecution for the act or omission has been initiated
-- against the employee, employer or other person; or (b) 36 months have passed since the day on which the act or omission
-- occurred." Thirty-six months have passed once the day is after the day 36 months on from the act (fork ei2-F10).
-- src:865 | Limitation on imposition of penalties
-- src:866 | 40 A penalty shall not be imposed under section 38 or 39 if
-- src:867 | (a) a prosecution for the act or omission has been initiated against the employee, employer or other person; or
-- src:868 | (b) 36 months have passed since the day on which the act or omission occurred.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 40 (src:865-868)
GIVEN `a prosecution for the act or omission has been initiated against the employee, employer or other person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day on which the act or omission occurred` IS A DATE
      `the day on which the penalty would be imposed` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 40 a penalty shall not be imposed` IF
       `a prosecution for the act or omission has been initiated against the employee, employer or other person`
    OR `the day on which the penalty would be imposed` ABOVE (`add months` `the day on which the act or omission occurred` 36)

-- 41: "The Commission may rescind the imposition of a penalty under section 38 or 39, or reduce the penalty, on the
-- presentation of new facts or on being satisfied that the penalty was imposed without knowledge of, or on the basis of a
-- mistake as to, some material fact." The satisfaction is the Commission's: a BOOLEAN input.
-- src:869 | Rescission, etc., of penalty
-- src:870 | 41 The Commission may rescind the imposition of a penalty under section 38 or 39, or reduce the penalty, on the presentation of new facts or on being satisfied that the penalty was imposed without knowledge of, or on the basis of a mistake as to, some material fact.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 41 (src:869-870)
GIVEN `new facts have been presented` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Commission is satisfied that the penalty was imposed without knowledge of, or on the basis of a mistake as to, some material fact` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 41 the Commission may rescind the imposition of the penalty, or reduce it` IF
       `new facts have been presented`
    OR `the Commission is satisfied that the penalty was imposed without knowledge of, or on the basis of a mistake as to, some material fact`

-- 41.1(1): "The Commission may issue a warning instead of setting the amount of a penalty for an act or omission under
-- subsection 38(2) or 39(2)." The power exists where the Commission could set a penalty for the act or omission.
-- src:871 | Warning
-- src:872 | 41.1 (1) The Commission may issue a warning instead of setting the amount of a penalty for an act or omission under subsection 38(2) or 39(2).
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 41.1(1) (src:871-872)
GIVEN `the Commission could set the amount of a penalty for the act or omission under subsection 38(2) or 39(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 41.1(1) the Commission may issue a warning instead of setting the amount of a penalty` IF
    `the Commission could set the amount of a penalty for the act or omission under subsection 38(2) or 39(2)`

-- 41.1(2): "Notwithstanding paragraph 40(b), a warning may be issued within 72 months after the day on which the act or
-- omission occurred." The 72nd month-anniversary counts (the keel's fork F4, and ei2-F10 here).
-- src:873 | Limitation period
-- src:874 | (2) Notwithstanding paragraph 40(b), a warning may be issued within 72 months after the day on which the act or omission occurred.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 41.1(2) (src:873-874)
GIVEN `the day on which the act or omission occurred` IS A DATE
      `the day on which the warning would be issued` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 41.1(2) a warning may be issued on the day` IF
    `the day on which the warning would be issued` AT MOST (`add months` `the day on which the act or omission occurred` 72)
